{5000}{}{[Wasteland Voices v1.0.0 active]}
{5001}{}{[Contour 1 (Core RPU): Active]}
{5002}{}{[Contour 2 (Extended Wasteland): Active]}
{5010}{}{Boot has another hole. Wade into the swamp after golden geckos and my toes rot right off.}
{5011}{}{Gecko skins are cheap as dirt now. Soon you won't barter a bowl of Buckner stew for one.}
{5012}{}{Heard scratching under town? Rats down there are fat as brahmin. Mean as hell, too.}
{5013}{}{Trap rusted shut. Needs fat, but all the fat went into Bob's still.}
{5014}{}{Whiskey Bob makes stout rotgut. Three mugs in, you understand what brahmin are mooing about.}
{5015}{}{Somebody got their ribs cracked at Golden Gecko yesterday. Drunk trappers brawling over beaver tail.}
{5016}{}{Drinking Smiley's gut-wash? Don't strike a match near your mouth or you'll torch the street.}
{5017}{}{Torr's crying about bug-men in the pastures again. Poor boy's mind is completely gone.}
{5018}{}{Dunton brothers sniffing around the herds. Never roll dice with them -- their bones are loaded.}
{5019}{}{Word is slavers down in the Den pay hard coin for able bodies. Stay off the south road.}
{5020}{}{Sulik the tribal is still working off debt at Buckner's. Mutters about his grandpa's bone. Creepy guy.}
{5021}{}{Wind's blowing hard off the canyon today. Bad sign. Smells like carrion and old dust.}
{5022}{}{Vic headed down to the Den three weeks back and vanished. Metzger probably sold him off for scrap.}
{5023}{}{Spot a fire gecko out in the wastes? Don't rub your eyes, kid. Drop your pack and run like hell.}
{5024}{}{Line at the bathhouse again. Trappers brought swamp lice into town, and lye soap is all gone.}
{5025}{}{Buy some dried meat, stranger. Smells foul, but keeps your gut from growling through the night.}
{5030}{}{Don't stand so close, kid. In the Den, folks slit throats for crumpled dollars without blinking.}
{5031}{}{Keep a hand on your pouch. Flick's brats will snatch ammo right out of your pockets while you yawn.}
{5032}{}{Metzger woke up in a foul mood. Flogged two runaways to death by breakfast.}
{5033}{}{Jet... just need one hit, just one... Lord, my bones feel like they're on a medieval rack...}
{5034}{}{Becky runs a fair wheel. Funny how everybody walks out of her casino in their underwear though.}
{5035}{}{Frankie cuts his rotgut with brahmin piss. Cheap though -- burns straight through your guts.}
{5036}{}{Gunshots down at the junkyard again. Lara and Tyler fighting over some stash, no doubt.}
{5037}{}{Smitty tinkering with that ancient wreck. People swear that metal heap used to roll without brahmin.}
{5038}{}{Ghost whispers in that ruin at night... weeping for a locket. Bah, junkies seeing shadows.}
{5039}{}{Watch your boots. Mud out here is loaded with rusty needles and rotting rat carcasses.}
{5040}{}{Slaver brand on your forehead is a death sentence up north. They feed you buckshot on sight.}
{5041}{}{Mom cooks stew from whatever's scraped off the dirt. Never ask what kind of bones are in the pot.}
{5042}{}{Drunk guard fell facedown in the ditch last night. By dawn, they'd stripped his boots clean.}
{5043}{}{Slaver guild hauls off all the able youth. Soon there won't be anyone left outside but crones and cripples.}
{5044}{}{Tubby gouges prices on 10mm rounds. Complain, and his thugs rack their shotgun slides.}
{5045}{}{Looking for a bed? Sleep with one eye open and your knuckles wrapped around a knife.}
{5050}{}{Dirt's dry as ash. Rain doesn't fall by autumn, we slaughter the breeding bulls.}
{5051}{}{Grisham gouges on slaughter fees again. Cheap old bastard squeezes every nickel till it bleeds.}
{5052}{}{Balthas's tannery stinks up the whole town. Gotta wrap a rag round your face just to breathe.}
{5053}{}{Heard about the Ghost Farm up northeast? Folks say glowing corpses burn with cold blue fire at night.}
{5054}{}{Someone dropped a watch down the town well. Kids climbed in, got stuck in the muck, barely pulled 'em out.}
{5055}{}{Rose fries the best omelet for fifty miles. Eggs are mighty huge though... unnatural big.}
{5056}{}{Wild dogs tore up two calves on the north range last night. Time to grab rifles and hunt the pack down.}
{5057}{}{Vault City traders treat us like manure under their boots. Slick bastards in their fancy blue suits.}
{5058}{}{Blacksmith bent an axle on the grain cart. Waiting on spare parts out of Redding going on two weeks.}
{5059}{}{Karl skipped town. Got tanked on rotgut and staggered toward the Den. Buzzards picked him clean, bet on it.}
{5060}{}{Corn tastes bitter this season. Ground water's souring again, picking up old poison.}
{5061}{}{Heading near the outhouse pit? Don't strike a match. Methane will blow you halfway to Klamath.}
{5062}{}{Jo buys grain for pennies and charges triple for ammo. Robber doesn't even need a gun.}
{5063}{}{Wind howls across the scrub at night. Lonely country when it's miles of dead sand all around.}
{5064}{}{Grisham's boy mopes around like he swallowed a live mole rat. Sour look on him all day.}
{5065}{}{Don't take kindly to drifters here. Too many jackals wandering the trail looking for an easy mark.}
{5070}{}{Step aside, Out-Sider. Your filthy rags offend the sterile purity of our complex.}
{5071}{}{First Citizen Lynette knows how to maintain order. Tribals belong outside the inner gate.}
{5072}{}{Those Gecko ghouls are contaminating our underground aquifers with their leaking reactor!}
{5073}{}{The Auto-Doc in Dr. Troy's clinic is a medical miracle. Extracts tumors in five flat minutes.}
{5074}{}{Servants from the allocation center work quietly and efficiently. No backtalk, only duty.}
{5075}{}{Was your rad count logged at the gate? We do not tolerate contaminated wanderers on our avenues.}
{5076}{}{Brawl in the Courtyard again. Barbarians lack the mental faculties for civil dispute.}
{5077}{}{Captain Gregory drills the guards with iron discipline. Laser carbines charged at all times.}
{5078}{}{Out-Siders think they can earn Citizenship via the exam? Laughable. Their brains lack logic.}
{5079}{}{Synthesized rations from food dispensers have optimal protein balance. None of that greasy brahmin slop.}
{5080}{}{That Courtyard junker tried selling me radio valves. Corroded scrap fished out of old dumps.}
{5081}{}{No random names in the Citizen Registry. Every lineage is vetted by mainframe algorithms.}
{5082}{}{Pitiable seeing tent-dwellers outside the perimeter. But sympathy cannot compromise our security.}
{5083}{}{Officer Stark is compiling recon on raider encampments. Our patrols will sterilize that sector soon.}
{5084}{}{Do not touch the City Network terminal, Out-Sider. That is property of the Citizen Council.}
{5085}{}{Order and law. Without Vault walls, humanity would have drowned in its own radioactive mire.}
{5090}{}{Reactor's rattling again. Coolant loop three pressure is spiking and the reservoir is dry.}
{5091}{}{Harold is a decent old skin, even with that damn tree sprouting out of his skull. Keeps us alive.}
{5092}{}{Vault City snobs pray for the day they can wipe us out. Terrified we'll leak radiation on their haircuts.}
{5093}{}{Flesh itches like crazy today. Soaked up a few dozen extra rads patching that steam flange.}
{5094}{}{Festus is cussing at the master console. Says without that Vault hydro-regulator, the core is toast.}
{5095}{}{Skeeter can patch any piece of scrap in his garage. Just don't stand near him while he's welding copper.}
{5096}{}{Woody serves beer warm and smelling of sulphur. Beats drinking sludge from the cooling pool though.}
{5097}{}{My eyelid slipped off into my mug last week... Rinsed it with moonshine and stuck it back on. Happens.}
{5098}{}{Lenny mumbles about some ancient Vault Dweller. Swears he shook his hand a century ago. Senile rot.}
{5099}{}{Radiation doesn't kill us, smoothskin. Just teaches you to get real comfortable with constant pain.}
{5100}{}{Junkyard is our bread and butter. You can dig up copper conduits and pre-war relays if you got patience.}
{5101}{}{If the core blows, Vault City won't survive either. East wind will blow their sterile paradise straight to hell.}
{5102}{}{Heard about glowing ones worshipping the subterranean reactor? Whining about Renewal. Lunatics.}
{5103}{}{Lost my nose twenty years back. Cried at first, but now it's handy -- can't smell the sulphur fumes.}
{5104}{}{Caravaneers hate stopping here. Think we glow in the dark and chew raw brahmin guts for breakfast.}
{5105}{}{We leave folks alone so long as they don't point rifles at our doors. Just let Gecko be.}
{5110}{}{Coughing up grit since sunrise. Dust down in the drift is thick enough to swallow lantern light.}
{5111}{}{Kokoweef miners brawled with Morningstar crews again. Sheriff barely broke it up before lead flew.}
{5112}{}{Jet is choking this camp. Half the drift crews can't even lift a pick without their morning puff.}
{5113}{}{Marge LeBarge pays hard coin for ore, but local store shelves suck every buck right back out.}
{5114}{}{Sheriff Marion's grim as a gravestone. Says if we don't clean house, outsiders will do it with rope.}
{5115}{}{Malamute Saloon is packed wall-to-wall. Miners dumping raw gold dust right across the roulette wheel.}
{5116}{}{Chems roll in from New Reno every week. Mordino crime family wants to grab every shaft in town.}
{5117}{}{NCR promises law and order if we join the Republic. We know their order: crushing taxes and gibbets.}
{5118}{}{Gold grit buried under my fingernails. Even the sourdough loaves crunch like sand between your teeth.}
{5119}{}{Monsters nested down in the Wanamingo mine. Big slithering claws... Nobody dares go down that hole.}
{5120}{}{Doc Johnson patches whatever's broke: crushed limbs or Jet shakes. So long as your coin is good.}
{5121}{}{Mordino muscle and Bishop's suit-men staring each other down at the bar. Blood's gonna spill soon.}
{5122}{}{Pick is blunt, spine is wrecked. Still gonna dump half my paycheck on cards before midnight.}
{5123}{}{Watch your step out there. A miner tweaking on Jet won't tell his own brother from a highwayman.}
{5124}{}{Vault City caravans haul in pills and haul out pure gold bullion. Legalized highway robbery.}
{5125}{}{Hear that whistle? Work in the drift is done. Mean, tired bastards with dynamite in their pockets heading up.}
{5130}{}{Watch your boots, hick. In New Reno, lead punches through your skull before your wallet clears leather.}
{5131}{}{Four families choke this town: Salvatore, Bishop, Mordino, Wright. Cross any, you end under the golf course.}
{5132}{}{Salvatores pack laser heaters. They say red beams slice wiseguys in half right on the open boulevard.}
{5133}{}{They drown card sharks in cesspools behind the Desperado. Only trusted Mordino boys deal the deck.}
{5134}{}{Corsican Brothers are hunting fresh flesh for their smut reels. Pretty mug can pocket a couple hundred.}
{5135}{}{The Wright clan distills top-shelf hooch. Old Orville despises Jet, but his alcohol flows like rivers.}
{5136}{}{Second Street junkies stacked like cordwood. Myron's Jet fries a man's grey matter in two fast months.}
{5137}{}{NCR congress-hounds prowling Bishop's Shark Club. John Bishop is aiming high -- straight for governorship.}
{5138}{}{Don't mess with trenchcoats and fedoras. Salvatore button-men itch to squeeze triggers on strangers.}
{5139}{}{Masticator broke a contender's jaw at the Jungle Gym. Scrubbed tooth chips and blood off canvas till dawn.}
{5140}{}{Hookers in the alley carving each other with broken necks over tricks. Welcome to the brightest pit on earth.}
{5141}{}{Tommy guns rattle every midnight. Hearse driver is running the most profitable racket in New Reno.}
{5142}{}{Renesco behind the pharmacy counter is sour as bile. Ask him for aspirin, he curses your entire bloodline.}
{5143}{}{Hit a jackpot at Shark Club? Don't stroll out the front arch. Shiv-artists already wait in the alley.}
{5144}{}{Myron keeps a stable of test-slaves locked down. Boy's a chem genius, but rotten to the core.}
{5145}{}{New Reno never sleeps. Folks check out here with showtunes playing and suckers clapping.}
{5150}{}{The village well is dry dust. Yesterday the bucket dragged up nothing but gray river silt.}
{5151}{}{Another yearling died along the fence. Flesh smells bitter from drought; unfit to roast.}
{5152}{}{The Elder sits by smoke all night. Says ancestors turned their faces from our people.}
{5153}{}{Hakunin boils root mash in his tent. Stench burns your eyes clean across the canyon.}
{5154}{}{Stinging ants swarm the lower canyon rocks. My brother barely dragged his legs back last hunt.}
{5155}{}{If the Chosen fails to find the GECK, we chew boiled scabbards and harness leather come frost.}
{5156}{}{Vault totems fade in the sun. Old songs say Holy Thirteen flowed with endless sweet water.}
{5157}{}{Flint point chipped on a radscorpion shell. Got to scrape another spearhead from river rock.}
{5158}{}{Coyotes screamed along the ridge at moonrise. Shaman says hungry ghost-blood is weeping.}
{5159}{}{Broc flower petals wither thin as skin. Healing brew turns out watery and weak this moon.}
{5160}{}{Heat split my hunting bow. Gut-string snapped right as a golden gecko broke from brush.}
{5161}{}{Smiths say scrap-iron is gone. Every new javelin is carved from bleached brahmin bone.}
{5162}{}{Mind your moccasins on the path. Canyon scorpions nest deep under sun-baked flat-stones.}
{5163}{}{Hakunin is out talking to squash vines again. Strange old bird hears voices in the leaves.}
{5164}{}{Spot Nagor, tell him Smoke tore through drying racks again. Dog needs a stout switch.}
{5165}{}{Scorching gale off south wastes. Old tales swear metal beasts roam those burnt lowlands.}
{5166}{}{Heed the Elder's proverb: Out-landers beyond the gorge carry poison tongue and sharp knives.}
{5167}{}{Dug up a spent brass casing in dry gravel. Relic from the holy Vault Dweller's first trail.}
{5168}{}{Thirst scorches throat since first light. Council rations water by single horn cup at noon.}
{5169}{}{May spirits shield the tribe. Without holy Thirteen, our bones crumble to canyon sand.}
{5170}{}{Air scrubber choked in the drift again. Down there without charcoal filters, lungs fry in an hour.}
{5171}{}{Marcus keeps a lid on this pressure cooker. Without his minigun, muties and smoothskins tear each other apart.}
{5172}{}{Uranium ore is rough trade. Hands don't glow, but teeth rot out of your gums before forty.}
{5173}{}{Don't spit 'meathead' at a super mutant unless you fancy wearing your ribs inside out, kid.}
{5174}{}{Typhon babbles about buried caps all afternoon. Old ghoul's grey matter has dry rot.}
{5175}{}{Miners grumble muties get prime meat rations. Morons forget muties haul boulders three times their size.}
{5176}{}{Miners' guild barking at city hall again. Going to settle shift pay with spade handles soon.}
{5177}{}{Broke a traveling guard's snout at Phil's taphouse last night. We don't take kindly to agitators.}
{5178}{}{One mercy: super muties don't guzzle hooch by the gallon. Town would have burned down years ago.}
{5179}{}{Heading down to lower stopes? Fasten your respirator. Radon gas pools heavy in the sump.}
{5180}{}{Marcus preaches we're building a new world. Sure hope I live long enough to draw breath in it.}
{5181}{}{Vault City pack train is late. Lynette's council pinching pennies over raw yellowcake again.}
{5182}{}{Ghouls shrug off rad-seeps in the shaft. Shame their knee joints turn to chalk while digging.}
{5183}{}{Whispers about bigots scheming against mutants? Sheriff has his eye on two loudmouths already.}
{5184}{}{Seymour the hound by the well has more wits than half the crew on the winch. Gospel truth.}
{5185}{}{Grit grinds between teeth dawn to dusk. Even pump water tastes like iron oxide and sulphur.}
{5186}{}{The old Master promised mutants eternity. Handed us wheelbarrows and uranium pickaxes instead.}
{5187}{}{Watch out under that ore hoist, traveler. Cable's frayed; snaps, and you're pancake gravy.}
{5188}{}{NCR merchants offer double for refined fuel ingots compared to those skinflints in Vault City.}
{5189}{}{Peaceful so long as the sump engines turn. Blowers fail, and this hole turns into suffocation hell.}
{5190}{}{Holster that sidearm, citizen! NCR has strict statutes. You're not in the lawless waste now.}
{5191}{}{President Tandi governs with an iron hand. Under her watch, Shady Sands built the Republic.}
{5192}{}{Senate raised grazing tariffs on longhorns again. Cattle barons are grinding their bowies.}
{5193}{}{NCR Rangers wiped a slaver outfit south of town last week. Scum deserved every hollow-point.}
{5194}{}{Baron Westin grazes the finest herds, but the old gentleman's ticker is skipping beats lately.}
{5195}{}{Congress debates annexing Redding. Without gold bullion, the Republic can't feed northern garrisons.}
{5196}{}{Dusty pours standard beer. Certified zero rads, no brahmin swill -- brewed to health code.}
{5197}{}{Stay clear of Bishop's New Reno lobbyists. Sleaze-merchants trying to grease senatorial palms.}
{5198}{}{Courts and statutes govern here. Steal a single brass shell, you break basalt on chain gang.}
{5199}{}{Baron Carlson bolted inside his manor. Terrified of western hitmen sneaking through the gate.}
{5200}{}{Ranger recruiting desk is open. Slaver-hunting is clean work, but damn near suicidal.}
{5201}{}{Vault City looks down their noses at our constitution. We'll see how high and mighty they feel soon.}
{5202}{}{Dr. Henry brews strange tonics in his lab. Rumor says he's engineering cures for mutant strain.}
{5203}{}{Keep travel papers dry. Without an entry permit, sheriff's deputies run you outside before sunset.}
{5204}{}{Drought choking outer farms. Don't tap new aquifers soon, ration coupons start next month.}
{5205}{}{Constables won't take bribes. Wave dirty scrip at an officer, you'll see the lockup from inside.}
{5206}{}{Bazaar's jammed shoulder-to-shoulder. Freight trains roll all the way from the Hub and Modoc.}
{5207}{}{NCR charter guarantees rights for every soul. Just happens rich cattle barons can afford extra.}
{5208}{}{Paved limestone avenues... My grandfather roaming the mud never dreamed civilized streets existed.}
{5209}{}{Button your coat near the gate market. Lots of slick drifters looking to pick a lining.}
{5210}{}{Back away from the shanties! We're scraping bottom ourselves; no handouts for vagrants.}
{5211}{}{NCR wants to seize our Vault. Wrap it in pretty legal statutes, but it's pure armed eviction.}
{5212}{}{Sump generator down below gave out again. Been burning scavenged tallow in the dark three weeks.}
{5213}{}{Voices echo from the cave jaw after dusk. Darion's raiders holed up down there... vicious bastards.}
{5214}{}{My young one hacks blood from cave damp. No physician out here, just a crone boiling roots.}
{5215}{}{We laid these flagstones with bare knuckles. Won't budge an inch, whatever NCR senate decrees.}
{5216}{}{Darion bars everyone from the core computer deck. Word is the old warlord went stark raving mad.}
{5217}{}{Mole rats butchered our last yearling goat. Life on this slag heap gets sourer every moon.}
{5218}{}{Who invited you? Shady Sands snooper? Clear out before rock-slings crack your skull.}
{5219}{}{Roof drip tastes like iron scales. Fail to boil the cup, your guts will knot till you scream.}
{5220}{}{Khans hoard carbines and canned beef down deep. Toss gristle and moldy crusts to the shanties.}
{5221}{}{Rebecca wants treaties with the Republic. Squatters don't trust politicians wearing tailored ties.}
{5222}{}{Scraping down dark sub-tunnels. Things nesting in the collapsed drifts far worse than mole rats.}
{5223}{}{Darion catches wind you're asking after the vault seal, his raiders will peel your hide.}
{5224}{}{Every sheet of tin here was pried off the old bulkheads. We bled for this miserable roost.}
{5225}{}{Walk on in peace, traveler. No gold here, no rotgut. Just alkali dust and hungry bellies.}
{5230}{}{Do not recoil, human. Gruthar teaches our pack patience and mercy toward your fragile kin.}
{5231}{}{Our talons rend steel, yet our minds seek understanding, not the spilled blood of the weak.}
{5232}{}{The Overseer console is mute. Voice recognition components fused to slag many cycles past.}
{5233}{}{Gruthar speaks of fellowship: all sentient creations sharing the wide sky in brotherhood.}
{5234}{}{Goris roams the high wastes seeking lore. We ask the silent stone that harm does not find him.}
{5235}{}{Surface dwellers see only nightmares. They level muskets before our lips can shape greeting.}
{5236}{}{Our hatchlings decipher ancient script upon terminal glass within the vault archives.}
{5237}{}{The great blast door shields our nest from irradiated gales and the cruel hunters outside.}
{5238}{}{The virus remade our flesh and unchained thought. We are no Master's hounds; we are Gruthar's pack.}
{5239}{}{Tube lights sting our yellow eyes, yet sterile illumination is kinder than tomb-black caverns.}
{5240}{}{Enter in peace and share our warmth. Enter with malice, and ancient talons remember slaughter.}
{5241}{}{Hydroponic troughs fail for want of maintenance. We lack copper connectors and micro-relays.}
{5242}{}{The human refugees break bread in our chambers. In return, our hide turns away raiders.}
{5243}{}{Man's speech sounds soft compared to pack roar, yet words speak the same longing: survival.}
{5244}{}{Keep clear of the egg nests. The nesting brood-mother's fury outstrips any philosophical debate.}
{5245}{}{May your path be unclouded. Remember well: intellect weighs heavier than curved ivory fangs.}
{5250}{}{The Emperor observes all. His silicon computation steers the Shi through shifting tides.}
{5251}{}{Sheathe your crude steel, barbarian. Chinatown observes sacred ordinances of civic restraint.}
{5252}{}{Dr. Sheng locked his genetics bay again. Botanical spore trials make councilors nervous.}
{5253}{}{The Dragon claimed victory without landing one fist. Sublime mastery of flowing chi.}
{5254}{}{Shi biochemists synthesized dense polymer fuel. The bay region will soon bow for our kerosene.}
{5255}{}{The Valdez is a barnacled rust-bucket. Wonder those flea-bitten punks haven't scuttled it.}
{5256}{}{Hey jack, spare a smoke? Stuck on this hulk going stir-crazy watching surf rot the hull plates.}
{5257}{}{The Captain swills whiskey in the bridge. Says until the nav computer wakes, we're beached for good.}
{5258}{}{Don't poke around cargo hold lower decks without a flamer. Mirelurks and centaurs spawned thick.}
{5259}{}{Punks worship liberty, Shi worship order. That's why they got tiled palaces and we sleep on iron wire.}
{5260}{}{Hubologists hawking pamphlets on the concourse again. Promise neuro-cleansing. Cultist quacks.}
{5261}{}{Your neuro-levels are clouded by primitive engrams! Seek Zeta-alignment before AHS-7!}
{5262}{}{Great Father Hubb shall launch our star vessel to Quetzel! This scorched orb is doomed to decay.}
{5263}{}{Tithe five hundred hard dollars to the Church, and elevate your spiritual essence to AHS-2.}
{5264}{}{Hubologist sentries carry energized carbines. Better keep quiet about their purple robes.}
{5265}{}{Chinatown arms dealers stock prime coast ordnance. Gouge you blind on the barter though.}
{5266}{}{Spiced wok-oil and temple incense... San Francisco carries a different scent than the dry interior.}
{5267}{}{Lo Pan and the Dragon nurture bitter grudge. Sooner or later, blood will wash the central street.}
{5268}{}{Heard rumors of Enclave outposts up the coast? They say black vertibirds drop out of clouds.}
{5269}{}{Valdez hull groans with every high swell. Pray the double-bottom ribs hold through winter.}
{5270}{}{The Shi care nothing for drifters. Yield no tribute to the Emperor, you're dust under sandals.}
{5271}{}{Punks blast guitar squall across the harbor till 3 AM. Shi patrols threaten to ventilate their speakers.}
{5272}{}{Heavy turbines hum deep in Hubologist bays. Cult's rigging something nasty with that space shuttle.}
{5273}{}{Bay fog rolls in thick as curdled milk. Can't spot your rifle barrel ten paces ahead.}
{5274}{}{Emperor logic banks cannot be breached. Slicers poking around receive lead through the forehead.}
{5275}{}{Need fusion batteries? Hoard bullion. Shi merchants laugh at faded paper script.}
{5280}{}{Halt! Where is your uniform, trooper?! Sergeant Dornan will skin your rear raw for regulation breach!}
{5281}{}{Vertibird four needs turbine overhaul. Birds drink aviation spirit like water.}
{5282}{}{South tree-line covered by interlocking dual-plasma turrets. Any trespasser vaporizes on contact.}
{5283}{}{Comm-link to the Rig is crackling. Squall line over the Pacific is scattering our dish arrays.}
{5284}{}{Clear the tarmac apron! Rotor downwash will cook your dungarees before you smell kerosene.}
{5285}{}{Mess tech boiled synthesized ration bars again. Glue tastes like engine gasket rubber.}
{5286}{}{Techs fiddling with the main transformer. Coolant loops trip, this outpost goes sub-critical.}
{5287}{}{Recon logged Republic scout tracks in the scrub. Standing orders: fire for effect, zero questions.}
{5288}{}{Advanced Power Armor Mark II weighs fifty pounds, but tribal lead bounces like dried peas.}
{5289}{}{Dornan's on the warpath. Some recruit left solvent rags piled behind the ammo magazine.}
{5290}{}{We represent the legitimate United States Armed Forces. We will cleanse this continent of taint.}
{5291}{}{Security protocol is absolute. Misplace your keycard, you face court-martial before taps.}
{5292}{}{Hangar chief chewing out flight officers. Pilots pushing low-altitude runs until rotor bearings bake.}
{5293}{}{Fueling vertibirds is suicide detail. Twitch on that high-pressure valve, kiss your fingers goodbye.}
{5294}{}{Micro-fusion inventory came up three crates short. Someone's pocketing government munitions.}
{5295}{}{Savages in the bush haven't the faintest inkling of the firepower stationed inside this fence.}
{5296}{}{Perimeter sentry shift in the gale is brutal. Coastal grit grinding inside servo joints.}
{5297}{}{Dr. Schreber's running vivisections in the bunker vault. Sounds coming through vents turn your gut.}
{5298}{}{Every cotter pin here is logged in the Quartermaster ledger. Discipline ensures Enclave triumph.}
{5299}{}{Toggle that selector to safe, soldier. An accidental discharge puts you on latrine detail with a toothbrush.}
{5300}{}{President Richardson addresses staff shortly. We stand on the precipice of American restoration.}
{5301}{}{Curling's FEV strain is calibrated. The mainland shall be cleansed of genetic deviations.}
{5302}{}{Core pressure holds nominal. Marine sub-station bulkheads can withstand any ocean swell.}
{5303}{}{Mainland mutates are evolutionary dead-ends. Chromosomes shredded beyond moral relevance.}
{5304}{}{Dr. Curling hasn't slept in seventy-two hours. Reclaiming our heritage requires relentless labor.}
{5305}{}{Atmospheric rad count on the Rig reads absolute zero. We preserve unblemished human lineage.}
{5306}{}{Frank Horrigan passed through Section C. Steel decking shuddered beneath that titan's tread.}
{5307}{}{PoseidoNet links every operational orbital transponder. Nothing transpires beyond our purview.}
{5308}{}{Department heads squabbling over mainland land grants once purification protocol concludes.}
{5309}{}{Breaching outer decontamination airlocks invites immediate summary execution by guard detail.}
{5310}{}{Old Glory will unfurl above every continental precinct once more, from sea to shining sea.}
{5311}{}{Black-suited troopers don't debate. Transmit security credentials or clear the console corridor.}
{5312}{}{Environmental scrubbers report persistent saline fog encroaching upon upper flight deck tiers.}
{5313}{}{We are the constitutional successors of this republic. Outlanders are ghosts upon atomic ash.}
{5314}{}{Secret Service details flank the Chief Executive at every briefing. Protocol is inviolable.}
{5315}{}{Aerosol delivery vectors near final staging. We shall reclaim what our forefathers charted.}
{5320}{}{Hush, brother. Within the Abbey's cloister, loud breath insults memories of ancient scholars.}
{5321}{}{Transcribing volume three on pre-war electronics. Brittle leaves crumble under the stylus.}
{5322}{}{We boil ink from pine soot and hide gelatin. Script sits dark and heavy upon parchment.}
{5323}{}{Father Abbot kneels in the nave, praying for souls swallowed in the Great Deluge of Fire.}
{5324}{}{Abbey cellar vintage soothes bitter spirits. The trick lies in taking communion in moderation.}
{5325}{}{Found an illustrated nursery fable in an iron chest. Such innocent wonder before the firestorms...}
{5326}{}{Coastal tribes bring marsh herbs in exchange for our distilled fever salves. Honest trade.}
{5327}{}{Brother Vintner dozed off beside the oak press. Smells of fermented berries across the courtyard.}
{5328}{}{Scripture and manuscripts alone separate wandering men from wild beasts of the radioactive sand.}
{5329}{}{Tallow drips close to the margin. A scribe's quill must trace true; blotches are unforgivable.}
{5330}{}{Founders of our order sleep in the stone crypts beneath. Their quiet rest remains sacrosanct.}
{5331}{}{We bear no iron weapons. The preserved Word is our sole bulwark against a vicious world.}
{5332}{}{Novices carry casks from the hillside spring. Cold water here bubbles sweet and pure as tears.}
{5333}{}{A peddler offered brass ammunition for our celestial atlas. We barred the gate against him.}
{5334}{}{The bell tower tolls prime. Time to mount the transcription bench until dusk swallows the light.}
{5335}{}{Centuries of book dust dye our palms. A noble mark of stewardship for forgotten knowledge.}
{5336}{}{Seeking harbor from the night? Our reading hall welcomes pilgrims of gentle heart.}
{5337}{}{Knowledge multiplies grief, traveler. Yet without it, our wasteland drowns in feral barbarism.}
{5338}{}{Brother Lucas burnishes brass clasps on the encyclopedia. Patient work spanning many seasons.}
{5339}{}{The wilderness beyond reeks of cordite and strife. Here dwells the calm hush of ancient thought.}
{5340}{}{Great Water churns rough today. Waves are angry; silver fish dived deep to hide with spirits.}
{5341}{}{Bone barb snapped inside big sea-pike's jaw. Must carve fresh hook from gecko rib.}
{5342}{}{Sulik walked north trailing slavers for his sister. Tribal heart aches for our fierce warrior.}
{5343}{}{Shaman burns kelp on the salt-rock. Smoke hugs the dune grass -- gale winds coming fast.}
{5344}{}{Iron-clad slavers creep from south trails to drag cubs away in chains. Drive javelins into their throats.}
{5345}{}{Scent of charred drift-fish and hearth sparks wards off shadow creepers along the beach.}
{5346}{}{Surf spit up a rusted yellow-marked iron tub. Shaman warns: death breath sleeps inside that metal.}
{5347}{}{Sinew mesh holds tight, but sharp reef shells slice braids like obsidian blades.}
{5348}{}{Tribe daughters dig fat clams from tide-mud before the gray swell roars back.}
{5349}{}{Your garb smells of alien stone cities and gunpowder stench. Great Water dislikes such taint.}
{5350}{}{Old mothers sing: across the endless surge lies green soil where slavers never set claw.}
{5351}{}{Trackers hauled golden lizard hide to camp. Whole clan chews marrow around embers tonight.}
{5352}{}{Salt breeze cuts right through gut-cloaks. We warm knuckles over charcoal near the foam.}
{5353}{}{Fling no refuse near the sweet spring. Water sprite sours the pool if strangers show disrespect.}
{5354}{}{Harpoon shaft must balance straight as dawn light piercing the sea mist.}
{5355}{}{We chant grandfathers' melodies: when sky-fowls flocked in millions and skies weren't scorched.}
{5356}{}{Village curs bark at dunes after sunset. They smell waste wolves pacing the ridge.}
{5357}{}{Trade in good faith: unroll salt and knapped spear points. Printed paper has no meaning here.}
{5358}{}{Wet sand grinds beneath calloused heels. Soil of our fathers; we stay beside the breakers.}
{5359}{}{May the morrow swell fill our willow traps. May ocean gods watch our children.}
{5360}{}{Alert: airborne mutagenic spore saturation in Sector B exceeds federal threshold by 420 percent.}
{5361}{}{Cryogenic stasis integrity compromised. Pod bio-monitors running on degraded reserve power.}
{5362}{}{Frozen asleep for a century and a half... Good god, what happened to the world beyond these airlocks?}
{5363}{}{Hologram emitter flickers. Sanitation service personnel have been unresponsive since October 2077.}
{5364}{}{Botanical mutation specimens breached greenhouse containment. Defoliant dispersion required.}
{5365}{}{Environmental Protection Directive 08: chemical ordnance disposal schedule indefinitely suspended.}
{5366}{}{Magnetic core storage corroded. Pre-war biochemical research databases suffered sector decay.}
{5367}{}{Warning: hoist cable tension meters indicate critical metallurgical fatigue in shaft three.}
{5368}{}{Nutrient synthesizer dispenses gray protein slurry only. Characteristic sulphur odor noted.}
{5369}{}{Pneumatic sorting arm jammed during sterilization sequence in pathogen quarantine bay.}
{5370}{}{Who authorized manual pod atmospheric purge? That constitutes a class-A procedural violation!}
{5371}{}{Carnivorous botanical tendrils logged spreading through primary HVAC circulation conduits.}
{5372}{}{Facility backup capacitors depleted. Emergency lighting cycling on low-draw pulse cycle.}
{5373}{}{My lab colleagues... the indicator lights on every pod beside mine died decades ago.}
{5374}{}{Ozone and decaying vegetative compost smell has choked these corridors for over a hundred years.}
{5375}{}{Please present authorized federal agency credentials to initiate console diagnostics.}
{5380}{}{Vault City armored scouts rattled past again. Swore they'd torch our shanties if we don't clear out.}
{5381}{}{We just want to hoe corn in the dirt in peace. Who does our dirt-poor village bother?}
{5382}{}{Mole rats root through cabbage patches, but old Connar says they're neighbors and watchdog allies.}
{5383}{}{Those aristocrats in blue overalls spit on us. Never formed a callus on their soft palms in their lives.}
{5384}{}{Driven off this homestead, where do we crawl? Slavers on the north route will have irons on us by noon.}
{5385}{}{Connar scours the trails for rifles. What good are rusty pipe guns against Lynette's plasma squads?}
{5386}{}{Alkali soil resists crops; gotta carry ditch water bucket by bucket to keep seedlings green.}
{5387}{}{A big mole rat chased wild dogs off the goat pen last night. Ugly brutes, but sharp watchdogs.}
{5388}{}{You're not one of their Citizen inspectors, are you? Tell them we don't surrender our homesteads without blood.}
{5389}{}{Cracked knuckles bleed in the dust. Meanwhile Citizens inside the fence brush lint off velvet coats.}
{5390}{}{Kids dread wandering past the fence line. A patrol spots them, they're branded vagrant trespassers.}
{5391}{}{Whole camp dug the well for two months. Brackish water full of chalk, but wet enough to swallow.}
{5392}{}{Connar stands up for squatters. Without his grit, they'd have trampled our hearths into dust.}
{5393}{}{Boiled wild turnip... that's the whole banquet tonight. Pull up a crate if your belly's pinching.}
{5394}{}{We beg no charity from Vault City. We demand only to be left unmolested on this dirt patch.}
{5395}{}{Bless those who shield poor folk. Justice doesn't stop by these parts very often.}
{5400}{}{The new batch burns like molten solder in my veins... Give me another hit, just one breath, please!}
{5401}{}{Myron threw beakers at the lab crew again. Whines the beta chem makes test subjects too rabid.}
{5402}{}{Manure smell from pens gags you. Brahmin fumes pipe straight into distillation retorts.}
{5403}{}{Mordino goons pistol-whip anyone nearing the gate without a signed commissary pass.}
{5404}{}{Tremors in my knuckles won't stop. When's the next test dose? The tech promised an evaluation!}
{5405}{}{That Myron punk is a pure sadist. To him, we're two-legged lab mice bred in wire pens.}
{5406}{}{Two test cases in barracks three coded from cardiac arrest. Threw their corpses into the ditch.}
{5407}{}{They claim they're refining medicines. All I see are needles, cage wire, and shotgun bullies.}
{5408}{}{Sulphur and ammonia stink soaked into my skin so deep no lye soap will ever scrub it out.}
{5409}{}{Don't catch the guards' eyes. Standing orders to unload buckshot at the first twitch of trouble.}
{5410}{}{Humming in my ears like hornets rattling inside my skull. That's the side effect of batch 2-B.}
{5411}{}{Chemical freight from Redding docked on schedule. Lab stacks will be spewing fumes all night.}
{5412}{}{The Mordino family rakes in fortunes on junkie shakes. Cursed compound, cursed desert.}
{5413}{}{If you walk out past the wire alive, tell my sister on Second Street I'm never coming home.}
{5414}{}{Barrack planks vibrate when they fire the sub-floor centrifuges for chemical refining.}
{5415}{}{Nobody weeps for street drifters. Hauled us out here to burn out our hearts for fresh product.}
{5420}{}{Step lively, cargo! Stray half an inch out of formation, take buckshot through your ribs!}
{5421}{}{Sun's scorching today. Iron shackles chafed the skin on my shins clean down to raw marrow.}
{5422}{}{Metzger doles a hundred caps for prime tribal stock. Lucrative racket, if you don't mind dust.}
{5423}{}{Fast buck tried scrambling over the razor wire at dusk. Attack hounds tore him to strips.}
{5424}{}{Keep safety off, guard. These tribals rush the stockade together, nobody walks away.}
{5425}{}{Single tin cup of tepid water at noon. Tongue swollen so fat I can't form syllables.}
{5426}{}{Neck bands are cold-riveted shut. Won't pry 'em off without a cold chisel and five-pound maul.}
{5427}{}{Driving a batch south to the Den and Reno next week. Fresh muscle fetches triple at the auction block.}
{5428}{}{Burned our river lodges at first light... My children wept when dragged into the iron carts.}
{5429}{}{Waste no tears on primitives. Catch you in the gulch, they'd peel your scalp with chipped flint.}
{5430}{}{Reek of sweat, spilled plasma, and glowing branding irons. Standard morning at the pens.}
{5431}{}{NCR Rangers scouting the ridgeline. Let them crawl down here; we've got full drums waiting.}
{5432}{}{Ancestors cannot hear our weeping over the harsh clatter of slaver iron.}
{5433}{}{Slaver goons tanked on rotgut by the coals, rolling dice for the prisoners' stew rations.}
{5434}{}{Hours drag like millstones. A bullet through the forehead on the trail beats this cage.}
{5435}{}{Eyes on the wire! Those wild bastards wait for a guard to nod off on watch.}
{5440}{}{Quiet on station, soldier. We operate behind hostile lines; excess noise draws scavengers.}
{5441}{}{Scoped hunting rifle zeroed at three hundred yards. Metzger's wolves won't know what punched through.}
{5442}{}{Scouts confirm an iron-chain convoy on the old north route. Ambush elements muster at dawn.}
{5443}{}{The Rangers swore an oath to crush slavery across the waste. We keep it down to our last round.}
{5444}{}{Wipe sand off that glass objective. Can't tolerate dust blurring the crosshairs.}
{5445}{}{This hideout is classified. Pick up a tail on the pass, circle through canyons until it breaks.}
{5446}{}{Every captive set loose lands a kidney blow against Den syndicates and Reno mobs.}
{5447}{}{Rations running thin, but Rangers are built to chew dried beef jerky on the march.}
{5448}{}{Staff brass in Shady Sands file paperwork. The real war for human liberty happens out in this grit.}
{5449}{}{Load soft-point rounds. Hollow core expands clean through boiled raider leather.}
{5450}{}{No smoky cook fires. In desert air, a column of wood smoke is visible for ten miles.}
{5451}{}{Death to slavers, freedom for the waste. A plain motto worth taking lead in the chest for.}
{5452}{}{Intercepted runner dispatches from the Den. Metzger's crews fear our crossfires worse than rot.}
{5453}{}{Cornered without extraction, bite the pill. You never surrender safehouse coordinates.}
{5454}{}{Actions oiled, shortwave dialed to distress band. Patrol squad ready to deploy.}
{5455}{}{Honor and law will triumph. The Republic endures while Rangers hold the outer perimeter.}
{5460}{}{Cold steel bulkheads rusted through. This warship is grounded in bay mud for eternity.}
{5461}{}{Torpedo tube two seized up on Great Flash Day. The warhead still rests silent inside.}
{5462}{}{Echoes through empty compartments? Fallen sailors whispering ancient oaths to the flag.}
{5463}{}{Shi repairmen trying to splice bus cables. Salt brine dissolved the copper two centuries ago.}
{5464}{}{Political officer ordered condition one battlestations... The order stands forever in the dark.}
{5465}{}{Condensation drips from command room ceiling. Drip... drip... counting dead iron centuries.}
{5466}{}{Bunker oil and salt weed stench baked into these rivets so deep nothing airs it out.}
{5467}{}{Nav dials calibrated for Beijing harbor. Cities across the Pacific turned to glass long ago.}
{5468}{}{Don't toggle master breakers. Residual voltage in emergency lines will scorch your heart.}
{5469}{}{We sailed to hostile shoals to fulfill our duty. Remained entombed in an iron vault under the bay.}
{5470}{}{Receivers pull only static hiss off the burnt coast. World above twisted beyond recognition.}
{5471}{}{Escape trunks dogged tight. Nobody on the surface will ever turn the outer wheel.}
{5472}{}{The Shi Emperor mainframe is flesh of our flesh, evolved from submarine navigation banks.}
{5473}{}{Shore crabs scuttle across flooded bilge grates. Life claws a foothold even down in the dark.}
{5474}{}{Watch officer's specter tours bilge posts at midnight, clutching phantom damage logs.}
{5475}{}{Rest in peace, sons of the Middle Kingdom. War concluded, though this iron whale never struck colors.}
{5500}{}{Giant beast nested in Trapper Town drifts. Trappers dread crawling down for pelt trapping.}
{5501}{}{Hear that squealing beneath floorboards? Under-rats are schooling up in packs the size of brahmin.}
{5502}{}{Crawling into Trapper Town tunnels? Pack a scattergun. Some giant rodent warlord rules down there.}
{5503}{}{A wharf rat chewed two toes off a sleeping skinner last night. Time to burn out that filth.}
{5504}{}{Rat God is butchered at last! Trapper Town skinners can string their leg-irons in peace.}
{5505}{}{Word is the tunnel beast stood tall as a grown man. Praise lead and powder it was blasted to bits.}
{5506}{}{With the big rat dead, the scuttlers scattered into the marsh. Town breathes easier today.}
{5507}{}{Trappers drinking to the underground monster's slaughter at Buckner's. Rotgut flowing freely.}
{5508}{}{Smiley hiked north to Toxic Caves three weeks back. Widow Buckner weeps into her aprons.}
{5509}{}{Green acid in Toxic Caves eats boot leather in minutes. Doubt Smiley walks out alive.}
{5510}{}{Maida's beside herself with worry. Her man vanished north, and golden lizards don't give quarter.}
{5511}{}{Spot Smiley in those caustic drifts, lend a hand. Though carrion birds likely picked him clean.}
{5512}{}{Smiley crawled out of caustic caves! Scored by acid, but breathing. Buckner wedding is on!}
{5513}{}{Folks swear a wanderer snatched Smiley right out of golden gecko jaws. Downright miracle.}
{5514}{}{Smiley is back on his barstool. Guzzling hooch and swearing off toxic holes forever.}
{5515}{}{Maida's grinning bright as polished brass. Her weeping stopped once her man walked through the door.}
{5516}{}{Poor Torr sobs in pastures. Someone rustles brahmin at moonrise and blames imaginary bug-men.}
{5517}{}{Dunton boys sell suspicious cheap flanks. Everybody knows whose brand was scraped off.}
{5518}{}{Duntons caught lead and a busted nose over rustled steers! Torr fears no shadows tonight.}
{5519}{}{Buckner herds graze without worry now. Cattle rustlers got taught a terminal lesson.}
{5520}{}{Torr lost the herd again... Town bullies mocked the poor boy till he ran crying.}
{5521}{}{Short on cows, Buckners must pinch pennies. Winter in Klamath is going to be lean and cold.}
{5530}{}{Metzger keeps trader Vic padlocked in back. Forces him to solder wireless sets at shotgun point.}
{5531}{}{Old Vic peddled broken tech to slaver captains. Now he pays his tab in collar iron.}
{5532}{}{Vic bought his freedom off the slaver block! Metzger ground teeth, but counted the gold clean.}
{5533}{}{Heard fat Vic skipped town with a wanderer. Lucky tub of lard to keep his hide intact.}
{5534}{}{Metzger's guild was wiped out! Slavers bleeding in the gutters! Merciful lord, is it real?!}
{5535}{}{Metzger got put down like a rabid mongrel. Auction pens are open and cordite hangs heavy.}
{5536}{}{Lara's gathering cutthroats at junkyard. Word is they'll storm Tyler's church warehouse.}
{5537}{}{Tyler's brutes guard chem crates. Lara pushes her luck, street turns into a butcher shop.}
{5538}{}{Church warehouse shootout concluded. Tyler's crew took dirt naps; Lara runs the stash now.}
{5539}{}{Grease guns rattled past midnight. Gravedigger hauled a cart piled high with stiff carcasses.}
{5540}{}{Lara's outfit got chewed to pieces at church gates. Tyler's handing out victory Jet to goons.}
{5541}{}{One gang drops, another rises... Signs change in the Den, but red mud tastes identical.}
{5542}{}{Ghost woman wails inside ruins after dusk. Weeping for a gold locket, scaring vagrants pale.}
{5543}{}{Steer clear of the burnt house at midnight. Dead Anna shrieks for her stolen heirloom.}
{5544}{}{Anna's specter sleeps at last! Locket laid in her grave, howling in the cellar died down.}
{5545}{}{Anna's bones got a decent Christian burial. Strange to find a sliver of mercy in this pit.}
{5550}{}{Glowing corpses impaled on stakes at Ghost Farm! Blue fire burns their bones; soil is cursed!}
{5551}{}{Modoc town council wants to muster militia and torch the Ghost Farm to cinder.}
{5552}{}{The Slags are no ghouls, but living folk! Signed a grain barter treaty with Modoc council!}
{5553}{}{Under-dwellers trade in open daylight now. Granaries will be full and crops protected.}
{5554}{}{Ghost Farm ran red with slaughter! Shotguns cleared the subterranean tunnels down to infants.}
{5555}{}{Butchery at the farm solved nothing. Crops torched; Modoc sits alone facing dry starvation.}
{5556}{}{Balthas lost his only boy. Little Jonny vanished, and Laddie the dog barks down the dry well.}
{5557}{}{Tanner is sick with grief. If Jonny tumbled down the masonry, he's crushed stone cold.}
{5558}{}{Jonny came home! The Slags kept him safe underground! Balthas is weeping tears of joy!}
{5559}{}{The boy is back hugging Laddie by the hearth. Entire street celebrating the little scamp.}
{5560}{}{Jonny is dead... Only a ragged child's coat fetched from the pit. Balthas is a broken man.}
{5561}{}{Sorrow hangs heavy over the tannery. Folks step softly around Balthas; pain's too raw to watch.}
{5570}{}{Poseidon core spitting hot steam! Third coolant conduit fails, atomic fallout cooks Gecko!}
{5571}{}{Vault City warns they'll shell us to gravel if coolant runoff keeps poisoning regional wells.}
{5572}{}{Hydro-magnet regulator seated in core! Reactor hums smooth and cool; rad levels dropped!}
{5573}{}{A wanderer tuned our plant without spilling a drop! Harold's buying rounds for the whole bar!}
{5574}{}{Vault City data disk patched the logic banks! Grid optimized; power enough for the north!}
{5575}{}{Vault City purchases our megawatts now! Ghouls and smoothskins bound by the same copper line!}
{5576}{}{Meltdown in sector four! Core burned straight to bedrock! Gecko is a glowing atomic tomb!}
{5577}{}{Death and hot cinder... Survivors fleeing into salt wastes, shedding skin as they sprint.}
{5578}{}{Vault City councilors furious: well monitors read clean; no excuse left to wipe out ghouls!}
{5579}{}{First Citizen council acknowledged Gecko's utility. Regional blackout crisis averted.}
{5580}{}{Lynette chews her lip raw: an out-lander brokered peace with muties she aimed to cleanse.}
{5581}{}{Captain Gregory doubled gate watches: peace with Gecko is uneasy; Citizens dread plague.}
{5600}{}{Air scrubber choked in uranium drift. Miners suffocating on radon gas; ore quotas ruined.}
{5601}{}{Lacking parts out of New Reno, shaft turns into a gas coffin. Marcus scouring trails for parts.}
{5602}{}{Scrubber purring like new! Intake blowers roaring; radon purged; picks striking yellowcake!}
{5603}{}{Refined ore trains rolling south again. Honest bullion clinking across Broken Hills counters!}
{5604}{}{Anti-mutant plot broken open! Franc and Manson behind bars; sabotage satchels defused!}
{5605}{}{Marcus preserved the peace. Human zealots sit locked down awaiting impartial magistrate trial.}
{5606}{}{Missing townsfolk found butchered in tunnels... Hate-mongers worked in dark to start blood.}
{5607}{}{Chad caught red-handed skimming caravan coin! Sheriff shook every stolen nickel from his coat.}
{5608}{}{Chad skipped across borders, ditching ledgers. Honest drivers cracking the whips on freight now.}
{5609}{}{Scrubber detonated by saboteurs! Drift collapsed; town robbed of commerce and bread.}
{5610}{}{Marcus fell in the dust... Town ripped asunder; men and mutants gutting each other on ruins!}
{5611}{}{Broken Hills is bleeding out. Without sheriff and ore hoist, only broken glass remains.}
{5620}{}{Fanged horrors breeding in Wanamingo shaft! Miners drop tools, refusing shifts at any wage.}
{5621}{}{Myron's Jet dropping drift-hands in heaps. Doc Johnson's clinic packed with foaming junkies.}
{5622}{}{Wanamingo brood-queen roasted to ash! Mayor auctioned shaft deeds; bullion flows again!}
{5623}{}{Wanamingo drifts sterilized clean! No slithering monstrosities dragging diggers into pits.}
{5624}{}{Doc Johnson mixed the Jet antidote cure! Shaking addicts sobered up and grabbed their picks!}
{5625}{}{Jet fever broken across town! New Reno's chemical leash snapped clean off Redding's neck!}
{5626}{}{Girl slashed open at Lou's saloon... Mordino thugs running wild; Sheriff barely holding line.}
{5627}{}{Blade-hound locked in cells for saloon carving. Law still carries teeth along these streets.}
{5628}{}{Rubble sealed the stopes. Addicts raided the depot; settlement sliding into lawless ruin.}
{5629}{}{NCR senate gearing for annexation. Without ore bullion, Republic won't bypass our borders.}
{5630}{}{Mordino cartel bought both mine gates. Miners swing sledgehammers for pinches of brown chem.}
{5631}{}{Vault City doctors arrived with medical bags. Charge indentured servitude for every sterile pill.}
{5640}{}{Chosen One entered the Temple. Ancestor spirits weigh his flesh and soul.}
{5641}{}{If the Chosen fails the Temple, wasteland sands will scour our tribe away.}
{5642}{}{Temple trials conquered! Holy Suit Thirteen gleams on the Chosen back!}
{5643}{}{The Elder handed down the holy Vault holodisk. Our fate walks south now.}
{5644}{}{The cistern is nearly dry. Children chew bitter roots; women weep by coals.}
{5645}{}{Without the holy GECK our tents will empty before frost. Time is dying.}
{5646}{}{Hakunin praises spirits: the foul weed-fiends were torn from holy soil.}
{5647}{}{The shaman brews healing powder again. Kettle reeks of bitter herbs and life.}
{5648}{}{Only blood and brass left in camp... Iron birds carried our blood south!}
{5649}{}{The gods abandoned Arroyo. Only cold ash and heavy combat boot tracks.}
{5650}{}{Old Orville is spitting rage. They find who sold Jet to Richard, blood floods.}
{5651}{}{Young Wright choked on foam in an alley. His brothers are loading shotguns.}
{5652}{}{Richard was poisoned by radscorpion venom! Chem peddlers lost all shame.}
{5653}{}{The Wrights bought the truth behind the boy death. Somebody head will roll.}
{5654}{}{Salvatore button-men swagger with their light-guns. Nobody dares breathe.}
{5655}{}{Mr. Salvatore choked in his sheets! His laser triggermen scattered like rats.}
{5656}{}{Bishop hiring mercs and eyeing the south. The Shark Club rakes chips in heaps.}
{5657}{}{John Bishop got butchered in his penthouse! War begins over his girls and felt.}
{5658}{}{Big Jesus cooks tons of Jet at the stables. Whole town hooked on his needle.}
{5659}{}{Big Jesus Mordino dropped dead of a seizure! Stables might get shoveled at last.}
{5660}{}{Heard? Some greenhorn had a shiny Chrysalis Corvega boosted off the tarmac!}
{5661}{}{That Corvega drifter ventilated chop-shop goons and drove his rig away.}
{5662}{}{Corsican Brothers hiring fresh meat for peep reels. Low pay, but wasteland fame.}
{5663}{}{New heavyweight champ at the Jungle! Knocked Masticator teeth into the ropes!}
{5664}{}{Do not idle under neon after dark. Catching lead in Reno is cheaper than water.}
{5665}{}{Jet addicts turning their pockets inside out in the ditch. Ugly damned town.}
{5670}{}{Vault 15 squatters barring Republic surveyors. Senate patience is wearing thin.}
{5671}{}{Darion raiders holed up in Vault 15 ruins. Caravaners dread that desert trail.}
{5672}{}{Vault 15 treaty ratified! Republic ore trains will roll through passes soon.}
{5673}{}{Darion and his Khans wiped out! The old raider ghost is purged from drifts.}
{5674}{}{A mole is nested in President Tandi staff. State dispatches leaking north.}
{5675}{}{The senate traitor was unmasked! Rangers tossed his chambers; spy in irons.}
{5676}{}{Westin herds are being rustled by the score. Ranch hands suspect desert beasts.}
{5677}{}{Westin grazing pastures sterilized! Not another twin-head steer vanished.}
{5678}{}{NCR Rangers posted bounties on slaver compounds. Big purge coming down the pike.}
{5679}{}{Slaver outpost north of town leveled to dust! Free citizens toast the Rangers.}
{5680}{}{Holster that hardware, citizen. NCR Marshals shoot to kill without polite words.}
{5681}{}{Tandi rules with iron grip, but senate taxes will strip homesteaders bare.}
{5682}{}{Shifty cutthroats pacing the outer Bazaar. Do not step past gates unarmed.}
{5690}{}{The Valdez rusts in dock slip. Lacking fuel and a nav-chip, she will not budge.}
{5691}{}{Tanker hold crawls with monstrosities. Upper deck punks fear climbing below.}
{5692}{}{Fuel surged into the Valdez tanks! Engine compartments humming, relief valves hot!}
{5693}{}{Tanker is rigged for sea! An out-lander patched navigation and turned screws!}
{5694}{}{The Dragon and Lo Pan drill fighters. Their bare-knuckle feud will burn town.}
{5695}{}{Lo Pan fell in honest ring combat! Dragon restored honor to the Shi dojos.}
{5696}{}{Dragon is dead... Lo Pan gloats; naked muscle and thugs dictate the avenues now.}
{5697}{}{Hubologists hawking in their palace. Promise clean zeta scans, just want coin.}
{5698}{}{AHS-9 butchered at the altar! Star cult scurrying to burn their fraudulent tracts.}
{5699}{}{The Shi Emperor decrees through terminal banks. No living soul saw his visage.}
{5700}{}{Badger girl hauled from the hold alive! The punk hacker is singing praises.}
{5701}{}{Shi chemists synthesize polymer skins and botanicals to purge poisoned dirt.}
{5710}{}{We just want to tend maize and live in peace. Why will not NCR leave us alone?}
{5711}{}{Darion festers in lower vaults dreaming vengeance. We dread his thugs worse than NCR.}
{5712}{}{Darion is dead! We are Republic citizens now; they promised dynamos and seed grain.}
{5713}{}{Sentient deathclaws guarding the holy portal... They speak with human tongue!}
{5714}{}{Gruthar speaks truth: his clutch seeks peace with mankind, not butchered flesh.}
{5715}{}{An out-lander repaired main mainframe! Egg nurseries cycling at full wattage.}
{5716}{}{The deathclaws were slaughtered... Cave floor slick with ichor and heavy brass.}
{5800}{}{Holy mother... What kind of walking turret is that?! Don't fire, iron demon!}
{5801}{}{Spirits of the ancients... The Steel Warrior walked down from the sky! Spare our hearths!}
{5802}{}{Look at that plate... My 10mm slugs would just bounce like copper sparks off that chest.}
{5803}{}{Display your ordnance registration for military-grade powered suit, citizen! Keep paws clear!}
{5804}{}{Hey hoss, sweat boiling inside that tin can? Look like you could walk straight through brick.}
{5805}{}{Salvatore button-men with their laser heaters will sweat bullets if you stroll into their pit.}
{5806}{}{Your boots rattle paving stones like forge hammers. Stepping off the curb before I'm flat.}
{5807}{}{They milled that armor pre-war for clearing concrete redoubts. Raider shivs won't scratch it.}
{5808}{}{Breathing meat inside there, or ancient cybernetic sentry running corrupt code? Terrifying.}
{5809}{}{Look here, sir... or ma'am... we're peaceful folk. Please don't trample down our shanties.}
{5830}{}{Hey! Drop that barrel toward dirt! One stray burst from that cannon shreds half the precinct!}
{5831}{}{Finger off the paddle, lunatic! Waving a flamer down a crowded avenue is suicide for everyone!}
{5832}{}{Sheriff! Madman prowling the boardwalk packing a six-barrel rotary! Run for cellars!}
{5833}{}{Toggle that safety on, traveler! Point that bazooka at empty sky; don't gamble with fates.}
{5834}{}{Marching for total war? That piece is built to split deathclaws, not browse marketplace stalls.}
{5835}{}{Lord, if that nozzle spits flame, my boots won't even survive the roast. Step the hell back!}
{5850}{}{Merciful lord... A genuine Master's super mutant! Keep that flesh-eater on a stout chain!}
{5851}{}{Keep that green mountain away from my porch! Brute could tear off my arm and never notice!}
{5852}{}{Marcus? Broken Hills sheriff touring our avenues? Sure pray that rotary is loaded blanks.}
{5853}{}{Phew, what rot! That ghoul reeks of unsealed crypts and embalming brine! Shove him outside!}
{5854}{}{Watch your boots, dead man! Chunk of dried ear just peeled off and bounced on the wood!}
{5855}{}{Who is that hooded giant? That's no man... he's got talons under those sleeves broad as sabers!}
{5856}{}{Monster lurking beneath that cowl! Caught a flash of cold slit-pupil eyes behind the cloth!}
{5857}{}{Your squad resembles a traveling sideshow freak tent. Hope your beasts are housebroken.}
{5880}{}{Oh, poor soul... Got no more wits than a boiled turnip. Take this rock candy and wander on.}
{5881}{}{Shoo now, simpleton. I haven't got shiny pebbles or sweet cane roots to barter for drool.}
{5882}{}{Look at that: can't string two grunts together without slobbering. Who let him roam loose?}
{5883}{}{Howdy, big guy! Fancy petting the heifer? Just keep thumbs out of her chops or she'll nip 'em.}
{5884}{}{Don't bray at me, primitive. Shoo off the boardwalk before you spook paying customers.}
{5885}{}{Poor jack, nature shorted you on grey matter. Don't touch that iron gear -- pinch your digits.}
{5886}{}{Speak slow, can't parse your hooting. Better yet, clamp jaws shut; folks might think you're wise.}

# ==============================================================================
# SLICE 4: EXTENDED WASTELAND QUEST STATES (5730-5778)
# ==============================================================================
{5730}{}{Now that the pump is running, we finally have clear water in the refectory. Blessings upon your hands.}
{5731}{}{The water filters are humming again. The Abbot calls it a true miracle of ancient engineering.}
{5732}{}{Pure well water without the taste of rust... We pray for the traveler who repaired our pump.}
{5733}{}{The beast in the wine cellar is finally dead. Now the novices can fetch barrels without their knees shaking.}
{5734}{}{They say nothing scratches in the cellars at night anymore. You saved our vintages from that fanged devil.}
{5735}{}{Brother James is pouring the Abbey brew again. Work goes a whole lot faster without a monster downstairs.}
{5736}{}{The printing press is back online! Soon we will finish copying the ancient medical treatises.}
{5737}{}{With the new gears, books no longer have to be scribed by flickering candlelight. A grand day for knowledge.}
{5738}{}{The press prints clean and true. The wisdom of the past will not turn to dust while our Abbey stands.}
{5740}{}{The well is brim-full of sweet water once more! The earth spirits have smiled on our tribe thanks to you.}
{5741}{}{The little ones no longer drink brackish swamp mud. The well water is cold and sweet, just like in elder times.}
{5742}{}{The shaman smoked the well stones with holy herbs. Now the water lends strength to our hunters.}
{5743}{}{Kooranna has returned to our hearth! Sulik's sister lives, and the cruel slavers could not break her spirit.}
{5744}{}{A mighty warrior delivered Sulik's sister home. The whole camp sings songs of praise for the Arroyo spirits.}
{5745}{}{Sulik and Kooranna sit together by the fire again. The sorrow that gripped our tribe has broken.}
{5746}{}{The merchant peddling his boom-sticks has packed up and left our shores. His dirty weapons no longer poison our traditions.}
{5747}{}{Spear and bow have fed our kin for generations. We do not need the iron toys of southern town-dwellers.}
{5748}{}{The shaman spoke true: bullet-mongers bring only spilled blood. Good riddance to that greedy outsider.}
{5750}{}{The predatory tendrils on the lower decks have withered. At least Sector B corridors aren't trying to eat you alive now.}
{5751}{}{The killer flora has been hacked to mulch. The air vents are no longer choking on toxic pollen.}
{5752}{}{Security holos report: botanical biomass in the bio-sector neutralized. Clean and efficient.}
{5753}{}{The cryo-pods are finally unlocked! People who slept for decades are breathing free air and heading north.}
{5754}{}{The freed captives still can't believe the old world burned to ash. But at least they walk free now.}
{5755}{}{The prisoners have vacated the subterranean vaults. This concrete tomb feels a little less dead now.}
{5760}{}{Connar handed out hunting rifles to every able body. Lynette's patrols will think twice before trampling our crops.}
{5761}{}{With real guns in our hands, we aren't Sergeant Stark's target dummies anymore. We will defend our roofs.}
{5762}{}{Vault City wanted to dump us in the radioactive wastes, but with rifles in hand, they have to treat us like men.}
{5763}{}{Thanks for the iron, wanderer. In these hills, folks only respect someone who can punch a hole through your knee at a hundred paces.}
{5770}{}{The slaver compound is reduced to cinder! Collars are smashed and Metzger's thugs are rotting under the desert sun.}
{5771}{}{We're free... Free! No more lashes, no more iron cages. We are taking to the high ridges!}
{5772}{}{The Rangers and a drifter from the west tore that butcher's pen apart. The Wastes are down a dozen bastards.}
{5773}{}{The slavers' blood soaked into the alkali flats. Honor to the guns that kicked down our pen gates.}
{5775}{}{Our scouts spotted a slave column east of the Den. We're setting up a dead-fall in the gorge.}
{5776}{}{The NCR Rangers keep their word: as long as we draw breath, man-stealers will not cross these passes.}
{5777}{}{Keep your rifle clean and your powder dry. The Waste does not forgive hesitation on the trigger.}
{5778}{}{Metzger thinks he owns the northern trade. Soon enough we will show his cartel what Republic law feels like.}

# ==============================================================================
# SLICE 4: ENHANCED MIRIA TRAVEL & CITY FLOATS (5900-5945)
# ==============================================================================
{5900}{}{Lord have mercy... The neon here is brighter than the Modoc fair, and the girls reek of sin from a mile off. Watch your pockets, darling.}
{5901}{}{New Reno... Father used to swear this pit would eat any country boy whole. Don't you go staring at those half-naked trollops, handsome!}
{5902}{}{Casinos, hitmen packing submachine guns, and the stink of Jet... Folks get butchered in broad daylight here. Let's finish quick and go.}
{5903}{}{Look at that: the Mordinos, the Bishops... mobsters at every corner. If one of them makes a move, shoot first; I've got your back.}
{5904}{}{Look how spotless it is... like an operating room. But they stare at us like we're roaches in their flour bin. Sterile snobs.}
{5905}{}{The 'Citizens' strut around in pristine jumpsuits while refugees outside starve in muddy rags. Makes my stomach turn.}
{5906}{}{That Lynette woman acts like she owns God's green earth. Back in Modoc, sticking your nose that high gets you dunked in the trough.}
{5907}{}{They've got a stamped form for every sneeze and breath here. You can't even spit without a council permit. I want out.}
{5908}{}{The air here smells like rotting meat and grease. Don't step two feet away from me, honey; these alley stares give me the creeps.}
{5909}{}{Slavers with brand marks right across their foreheads... They look at me like a heifer at an auction. It chills my blood.}
{5910}{}{Junkies tweaking on every corner and street urchins with shivs. Button your coat tight, they'll skin your boots right off your feet.}
{5911}{}{The Den sure earned its name. The sorriest cesspool in all of California. Let's wrap up our business and hit the road.}
{5912}{}{Home... Sweet Modoc! Smells like father's slaughterhouse and fresh straw. I can hardly believe we're back, darling.}
{5913}{}{There's Grisham's roof, and Rose's bed-and-breakfast... You know, I actually missed this dusty crossroads while we were wandering.}
{5914}{}{I hope father's health is holding up. Let's go check in on him, just holstered your piece first or he'll start bickering about the dowry.}
{5915}{}{Everything here is so simple and quiet. No bullets whistling past our ears, no monsters. Just good soil and hard-working folk.}
{5916}{}{Reeks of stale booze, harsh soap, and damp gecko hides. Father always said Klamath was full of drunks and poachers. He wasn't lying.}
{5917}{}{Trappers bundled up in greasy leather rags... Half of them can barely string three words together after Bob's moonshine.}
{5918}{}{Mind your footing, the mud is ankle-deep here. And oil your rifle action; this river damp will rust steel before nightfall.}
{5919}{}{Listen to that racket coming out of the Golden Gecko. I just hope we don't have to bust teeth over a spilled mug of draft.}
{5920}{}{Is that... the ocean?! Lord Almighty, it's enormous! More water than all the northern rivers poured together!}
{5921}{}{The Shi glide around in silk robes bowing to a mainframe Emperor, while tankers punks down rotgut on a rusted hulk... Miracles of the Wastes.}
{5922}{}{Those Hubologists in their shiny white smocks smell like a cult from twenty yards away. Don't swallow their star-babble, darling, they'll fleece you dry.}
{5923}{}{Salty wind, screeching iron cranes, and the aroma of grilled fish. A whole different world from our cattle pastures.}
{5924}{}{Mutants, ghouls, and humans sharing drinks at the saloon? Father would have grabbed his shotgun, but they're just mining uranium side by side.}
{5925}{}{Sheriff Marcus commands respect. Big as a hillside boulder, but speaks more sense than half the councilmen in California.}
{5926}{}{The air from the mine shaft smells of sulfur and crushed slag. It's a tough, gritty town, but folks keep order here.}
{5927}{}{The ghouls here aren't vicious like the horror tales say. You get used to their raspy voices once you talk a spell.}
{5928}{}{Everyone's hacking up phlegm, faces black with coal and gold dust... All anyone mutters about is dust and Jet. Bleak place.}
{5929}{}{The miners blow their whole week's strike at the roulette tables and Madam Lou's girls. Like moths diving into a torch.}
{5930}{}{Sheriff Marion looks like he hasn't closed his eyes in three weeks. This claim war between the mines will end in bloodshed.}
{5931}{}{This gold fever turns decent men into wolves. Let's settle what we came for and ride on; I can hardly draw breath here.}
{5932}{}{The Abbey... Quiet as a church before the lightning cracks. The monks scribing those giant books... Father would have loved their wine cellar.}
{5933}{}{The brothers live lean, praying to science and faded ink. A surprisingly peaceful corner in our scorched world.}
{5934}{}{That chapel bell ringing across the bluffs puts my heart at ease. At least somewhere out here isn't screaming with gunsmoke.}
{5935}{}{The EPA... Holograms? Man-eating vegetation?! Where in heaven's name did you drag me?! Back home the worst scare was a brahmin loose in the corn!}
{5936}{}{This research bunker feels like a madman's fever dream. Flashing dials, poison vapor, and dead nightmares waking up. Keep that gun up!}
{5937}{}{Don't get too close to those specimen tanks, honey! I swear that thing just twitched inside the brine...}
{5938}{}{A tribe living right against the tide... You know, they remind me a lot of your Arroyo kinfolk you told me about.}
{5939}{}{Hovels lashed from driftwood, bone fish-hooks... Humble folk, but they carry themselves with quiet pride.}
{5940}{}{Ocean surf and the smell of kelp. If Metzger's man-hunters weren't prowling nearby, this would be a proper slice of paradise.}
{5941}{}{Alkali grit grinding in my teeth... Darling, how much further across these badlands? My soles are worn paper-thin.}
{5942}{}{The canteen's half-empty. We'd best fill up our waterskins at the very next trader camp.}
{5943}{}{I never dreamed I'd marry a tribal scout and trek across the whole breadth of California. But you sure keep life interesting, handsome!}
{5944}{}{The wind died right down. That dead quiet always comes before a sand-squall... Tighten your pack straps, let's make tracks.}
{5945}{}{When we finally dig up that GECK of yours, we're building a proper ranch back on the flats and raising a dozen head of cattle, deal?}

